      "\"Social media management\" is one of the vaguest line items a small business ever pays for, because it can mean almost anything — from someone scheduling four generic posts a month with a stock caption, to a genuinely planned content and community strategy tied to actual business goals. The price varies enormously because the scope hides inside a single phrase.",
      "### What \"Social Media Management\" Actually Bundles Together",
      "Underneath the umbrella term, the real components are: content planning (what to post and why), design or video production for each post, actually publishing on a schedule, responding to comments and messages, and reporting on what's working. Different packages include different combinations of these five — the price tells you almost nothing until you know which of the five you're actually getting.",
      "### Entry-Level Pricing: What You Get and What You Don't",
      "The lowest tier typically covers scheduled posting only — a set number of posts per month, designed from a template, with little to no strategy behind what's posted or why. It rarely includes comment or message monitoring, meaning customer questions in your comments can sit unanswered for days. This tier can be a reasonable starting point for a business that just needs a consistent presence, but it won't meaningfully grow an audience or drive inquiries on its own.",
